{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/edgeColoring()"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge colouring with at most Δ + 1 colours (Vizing’s bound), by Misra and Gries’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constructive proof (Boost "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge_coloring"},{"type":"text","text":", rustworkx "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph_misra_gries_edge_color"},{"type":"text","text":", with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their own choices; Sage "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge_coloring"},{"type":"text","text":"). Edges in position order, each coloured through a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fan at its end with the lesser vertex index, every choice the least colour or vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"available. At least Δ colours always, and Δ + 1 on class-2 graphs (odd cycles, odd complete"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graphs, Petersen), but sometimes Δ + 1 on class-1 graphs too (K(4)); on a bipartite graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartiteEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":" always gives Δ. O(m · (Δ² + n)) time: a fan has at most Δ"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, each found among the edges at u, and a path at most n edges. O(n + m) memory."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a multigraph ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"digraph.undirected"},{"type":"text","text":" with an antiparallel pair is one), use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProto